71. Explain @Transactional internally.

   1. Spring uses proxy-based AOP to intercept calls to transactional methods.
   2. The transaction manager starts or joins a transaction.
   3. The method executes within the transaction boundary.
   4. Spring commits on successful completion or rolls back based on configured rollback rules.

